speechtext:
What are the names of the persons who will accompany the hon. Minister of Trade and Commerce on his mission to the United Kingdom this month?
Answer by: Hon. Gordon Churchill (Minister
of Trade and Commerce):
Canadian trade mission to the United Kingdom
The following have accepted invitations to be members of the Canadian trade mission to the United Kingdom, to be led by the Hon. Gordon Churchill:
James S. Duncan, chairman, Hydro-Electric Power Commission of Ontario, Toronto, and deputy leader of the mission;
Robert J. Askin, vice-president, Abitibi Power and Paper Company Limited, Toronto;
Questions
A.	G. Bailey, president, Bailey-Selburn Oil and Gas Limited, Calgary;
Lt.-Col. Herve Baribeau, president, Bari-beau & Son, Levis, Que.;
John L. Bonus, general manager, Canadian Association of British Manufacturers and Agencies, Toronto;
Lawrence C. Bonnycastle, vice-president and managing-director, Canadian Corporate Management Company Limited, Toronto;
Leonard W. Brockington, president, Odeon Theatres (Canada) Ltd., Toronto;
E. A. Bromley, vice-president, Canadian National Railways, Montreal;
J. Arthur Clark, president, Maritime Asphalt Products Ltd., Summerside, P.E.I.;
